@* The quiet zone is the empty border scanners need around the modules. Margin is drawn as CSS
   padding by the compiler; ShowMargin=false drops it, for a QR that sits flush against its
   surface — trade the quiet zone for space when the code is decorative, not scanned. *@
<div class="flex gap-4">
    <Card>
        <CardHeader><CardTitle Class="text-sm">With quiet zone</CardTitle></CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="flex justify-center p-4"><QrCode Value="https://lumeo.nativ.sh/" Size="120" /></CardContent>
    </Card>
    <Card>
        <CardHeader><CardTitle Class="text-sm">No margin</CardTitle></CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="flex justify-center p-4"><QrCode Value="https://lumeo.nativ.sh/" Size="120" ShowMargin="false" /></CardContent>
    </Card>
</div>
